                "projectEmailContents": {
                    "260715_SH01006.A.Project_Test-Libs6-2026-06-22_22.txt": "Dear ,\n\nSamples/Libraries submitted under Test-Libs6-2026-06-22_22 to NSC, Ullev\u00e5l has been sequenced and are now ready for pick-up. You will therefore be billed for this service.\n\n\n------ Data collection ------\nYou can pick up the data in a portable hard drive (please notice the size of the data  is approximately XXXX GB).\n\nNOTE: UNKNOWN Delivery method\n\nWe will keep a copy of the data for THREE MONTHS after the run date, and will then DELETE ALL OUR COPIES without further notice.\n\n\n------ Data output ------\nHere is an overview of your samples and the number of fragments that were sequenced:\n\n22-miseq22_L001                    \t       8,928 fragments\n21-miseq21_L001                    \t      60,579 fragments\n20-miseq20_L001                    \t      56,225 fragments\n19-miseq19_L001                    \t       5,107 fragments\n18-miseq18_L001                    \t      91,083 fragments\n17-miseq17_L001                    \t      53,043 fragments\n16-miseq16_L001                    \t       6,723 fragments\n15-miseq15_L001                    \t      66,354 fragments\n14-miseq14_L001                    \t      61,667 fragments\n13-miseq13_L001                    \t       5,480 fragments\n12-miseq12_L001                    \t      53,544 fragments\n11-miseq11_L001                    \t      41,226 fragments\n10-miseq10_L001                    \t      58,285 fragments\n9-miseq9_L001                      \t      67,839 fragments\n8-miseq8_L001                      \t      27,109 fragments\n7-miseq7_L001                      \t      46,829 fragments\n6-miseq6_L001                      \t      73,120 fragments\n5-miseq5_L001                      \t      79,096 fragments\n4-miseq4_L001                      \t      56,186 fragments\n3-miseq3_L001                      \t      92,156 fragments\n2-miseq2_L001                      \t      77,415 fragments\n1-miseq1_L001                      \t      70,859 fragments\n\n\n----- Bioinformatic analyses ----\nData alignment/analysis can be ordered as a service. For further details: http://www.sequencing.uio.no/services/bioinformatics/\n\nIf you have any questions, don't hesitate to get in touch. \n\n\n----- Technical details ----\nThe following run parameters and software versions were used to produce the data:\n\nSequencer Type: MiSeqi100Plus\n: \n\nMiSeqi100Plus System Suite: 1.1.0.26158\nBCL Convert: 4.3.6\nNSC scripts: 3.0\n\n\nRegards\nArvind Sundaram / Marius Bj\u00f8rnstad\n\nBioinformatician(s)\nNorwegian Sequencing Centre (https://www.sequencing.uio.no) / Part of NorSeq (https://www.norseq.org/)\nOslo University Hospital, Ullev\u00e5l, Oslo, Norway\n\n\n*********************************************************************************************************************\nUnderstanding the data: https://www.sequencing.uio.no/illumina-services/10.%20Bioinformatic%20services/#toc9\n\n------- Acknowledgement -------\nThe Norwegian Sequencing Centre (NSC) operates as a core facility and you will therefore not be billed for the labour costs incurred. However, you are requested to acknowledge the support you have received from the bodies funding the NSC. Please use the following text in articles or reports relating to this sequence data:\n\"The sequencing service was provided by the Norwegian Sequencing Centre (www.sequencing.uio.no), a national technology platform hosted by the University of Oslo and Oslo University Hospital, and supported by the Research Council of Norway and the Southeastern Regional Health Authorities\".\n\n-----Terms, conditions and usage-----\nData storage policy: https://www.sequencing.uio.no/illumina-services/10.%20Bioinformatic%20services/#toc12\nData security:  https://www.sequencing.uio.no/illumina-services/10.%20Bioinformatic%20services/#toc11\n*********************************************************************************************************************\n\n",
                    "Open_emails.command": "#!/bin/bash\n\n# This shell script is written to the Delivery folder in\n# all runs processed by the demultiplexing scripts. It calls the AppleScript file\n# \"Open Emails.scpt\", which is located in /data/runScratch.boston/scripts.\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=$( dirname \"$0\" )\ncd \"$SCRIPT_DIR\"\nfor list_file in automatic_email_list-*.txt\ndo\n    osascript /Volumes/runScratch/scripts/Open\\ Emails.scpt \"$SCRIPT_DIR\" \"$list_file\"\ndone\n",
                    "automatic_email_list-260715_SH01006.A.Project_Test-Libs6-2026-06-22_22.txt": "text|||\"nsc-ous-data-delivery@sequencing.uio.no\" <nsc-ous-data-delivery@sequencing.uio.no>|Sequence ready for download - sequencing run 20260715_SH01006_0020_ASC2245414-SC3 - Test-Libs6-2026-06-22_22 (22 samples)|260715_SH01006.A.Project_Test-Libs6-2026-06-22_22.txt|\n"
                },
                "runSummaryEmailContents": {
                    "Open_emails.command": "#!/bin/bash\n\n# This shell script is written to the Delivery folder in\n# all runs processed by the demultiplexing scripts. It calls the AppleScript file\n# \"Open Emails.scpt\", which is located in /data/runScratch.boston/scripts.\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=$( dirname \"$0\" )\ncd \"$SCRIPT_DIR\"\nfor list_file in automatic_email_list-*.txt\ndo\n    osascript /Volumes/runScratch/scripts/Open\\ Emails.scpt \"$SCRIPT_DIR\" \"$list_file\"\ndone\n",
                    "Summary_for_20260715_SH01006_0020_ASC2245414-SC3.html": "<!doctype html>\n\n<html>\n<head>\n<title>Run summary</title>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n</head>\n\n<style>\nbody {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n\ntable {\n    border-collapse: collapse;\n    margin: 5px;\n}\ntable, th, td {\n    border: 1px solid black;\n}\ntable.lims_info {\n    margin-top: 20px;\n    margin-bottom: 20px;\n}\ntd {\n    padding: 3px;\n}\ntd.number {\n    text-align: center;\n}\ntd.center {\n    text-align: center;\n}\ntd.text {\n}\n</style>\n\n<body>\n<table>\n<tr>\n\n    <th>Lane</th>\n\n    <th>Project</th>\n\n    <th>PF cluster no</th>\n\n    <th>PF ratio</th>\n\n    <th>SeqDuplicates</th>\n\n    <th>Undetermined</th>\n\n    <th>AlignPhixR1</th>\n\n    <th>AlignPhixR2</th>\n\n    <th>>=Q30</th>\n\n    <th>Occupied</th>\n\n    <th>Informative</th>\n\n    <th>MaxReadsSam</th>\n\n    <th>MinReadsSam</th>\n\n    <th>Quality</th>\n\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n\n    <td class=\"center\">1</td>\n\n    <td class=\"text\">Test-Libs6-2026-06-22_22</td>\n\n    <td class=\"number\">5,567,926</td>\n\n    <td class=\"number\">70.4 %</td>\n\n    <td class=\"number\">0.04 %</td>\n\n    <td class=\"number\">79.19 %</td>\n\n    <td class=\"number\">3.66 %</td>\n\n    <td class=\"number\">3.58 %</td>\n\n    <td class=\"number\">93.92 %</td>\n\n    <td class=\"number\">81.51 %</td>\n\n    <td class=\"number\">14.65 %</td>\n\n    <td class=\"number\">+75.0%</td>\n\n    <td class=\"number\">-90.3%</td>\n\n    <td class=\"text\">ok</td>\n\n</tr>\n\n</table>\n\n\n<h3>Run parameters</h3>\n<table>\n    <tr>\n        <td>Instrument</td>\n        <td>MiSeqi100Plus</td>\n        <td>SH01006 ()</td>\n    </tr>\n    \n    <tr>\n        <td>Cycles</td>\n        <td>R1</td>\n        <td>151</td>\n    </tr>\n    \n    <tr>\n        <td></td>\n        <td>I1</td>\n        <td>11</td>\n    </tr>\n    \n    <tr>\n        <td></td>\n        <td>I2</td>\n        <td>11</td>\n    </tr>\n    \n    <tr>\n        <td></td>\n        <td>R2</td>\n        <td>151</td>\n    </tr>\n    \n</table>\n<h4>Versions</h4>\n<table>\n\n    <tr><td>MiSeqi100Plus System Suite</td><td>1.1.0.26158</td></tr>\n\n    <tr><td>BCL Convert</td><td>4.3.6</td></tr>\n\n    <tr><td>NSC scripts</td><td>3.0</td></tr>\n\n</table>\n\n\n<h2>Projects</h2>\n\n<h3>Test-Libs6-2026-06-22_22</h3>\n<p>Sequence ready for download - sequencing run 20260715_SH01006_0020_ASC2245414-SC3 - Test-Libs6-2026-06-22_22 (22 samples)</p>\n<table class=\"lims_info\">\n    <tr><td>Contact person</td><td></td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Contact email</td><td></td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Delivery method</td><td></td></tr>\n    <tr><td>Directory name</td><td>260715_SH01006.A.Project_Test-Libs6-2026-06-22_22</td></tr>\n</table>\n<table>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>22-miseq22_L001</td>\n    <td>8,928 fragments</td>\n    <td>-83.1 %</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>21-miseq21_L001</td>\n    <td>60,579 fragments</td>\n    <td>+15.0 %</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>20-miseq20_L001</td>\n    <td>56,225 fragments</td>\n    <td>+6.7 %</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>19-miseq19_L001</td>\n    <td>5,107 fragments</td>\n    <td>-90.3 %</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>18-miseq18_L001</td>\n    <td>91,083 fragments</td>\n    <td>+72.9 %</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>17-miseq17_L001</td>\n    <td>53,043 fragments</td>\n    <td>+0.7 %</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>16-miseq16_L001</td>\n    <td>6,723 fragments</td>\n    <td>-87.2 %</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>15-miseq15_L001</td>\n    <td>66,354 fragments</td>\n    <td>+26.0 %</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>14-miseq14_L001</td>\n    <td>61,667 fragments</td>\n    <td>+17.1 %</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>13-miseq13_L001</td>\n    <td>5,480 fragments</td>\n    <td>-89.6 %</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>12-miseq12_L001</td>\n    <td>53,544 fragments</td>\n    <td>+1.6 %</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>11-miseq11_L001</td>\n    <td>41,226 fragments</td>\n    <td>-21.7 %</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n    <td>10-miseq10_L001</td>\n    <td>58,285 fragments</td>\n  