                "projectEmailContents": {
                    "260625_LH00534.A.Project_Example-test1-2026-07-28.txt": "Dear ,\n\nSamples/Libraries submitted under Example-test1-2026-07-28 to NSC, Ullev\u00e5l has been sequenced and are now ready for pick-up. You will therefore be billed for this service.\n\n\n------ Data collection ------\nYou can pick up the data in a portable hard drive (please notice the size of the data  is approximately XXXX GB).\n\nNOTE: UNKNOWN Delivery method\n\nWe will keep a copy of the data for THREE MONTHS after the run date, and will then DELETE ALL OUR COPIES without further notice.\n\n\n------ Data output ------\nHere is an overview of your samples and the number of fragments that were sequenced:\n\n5-e_L001                           \t 141,480,650 fragments\n6-f_L001                           \t  73,305,543 fragments\n7-g_L001                           \t  63,202,687 fragments\n8-h_L001                           \t  71,263,750 fragments\n9-i_L001                           \t 103,537,215 fragments\n1-a_L001                           \t  50,091,953 fragments\n2-b_L001                           \t  60,764,676 fragments\n3-c_L001                           \t 107,719,625 fragments\n4-d_L001                           \t  24,395,237 fragments\n\n\n----- Bioinformatic analyses ----\nData alignment/analysis can be ordered as a service. For further details: http://www.sequencing.uio.no/services/bioinformatics/\n\nIf you have any questions, don't hesitate to get in touch. \n\n\n----- Technical details ----\nThe following run parameters and software versions were used to produce the data:\n\nSequencer Type: NovaSeqXPlus\nFlow Cell Type: 1.5B\n\nNovaSeqXPlus System Suite: 1.4.0.20115\nBCL Convert: 4.3.6\nNSC scripts: 3.0\n\n\nRegards\nArvind Sundaram / Marius Bj\u00f8rnstad\n\nBioinformatician(s)\nNorwegian Sequencing Centre (https://www.sequencing.uio.no) / Part of NorSeq (https://www.norseq.org/)\nOslo University Hospital, Ullev\u00e5l, Oslo, Norway\n\n\n*********************************************************************************************************************\nUnderstanding the data: https://www.sequencing.uio.no/illumina-services/10.%20Bioinformatic%20services/#toc9\n\n------- Acknowledgement -------\nThe Norwegian Sequencing Centre (NSC) operates as a core facility and you will therefore not be billed for the labour costs incurred. However, you are requested to acknowledge the support you have received from the bodies funding the NSC. Please use the following text in articles or reports relating to this sequence data:\n\"The sequencing service was provided by the Norwegian Sequencing Centre (www.sequencing.uio.no), a national technology platform hosted by the University of Oslo and Oslo University Hospital, and supported by the Research Council of Norway and the Southeastern Regional Health Authorities\".\n\n-----Terms, conditions and usage-----\nData storage policy: https://www.sequencing.uio.no/illumina-services/10.%20Bioinformatic%20services/#toc12\nData security:  https://www.sequencing.uio.no/illumina-services/10.%20Bioinformatic%20services/#toc11\n*********************************************************************************************************************\n\n",
                    "260625_LH00534.A.Project_Testcase-test2-2026-07-28.txt": "Dear Thea Testcase,\n\nSamples/Libraries submitted under Testcase-test2-2026-07-28 to NSC, Ullev\u00e5l has been sequenced and are now ready for pick-up. You will therefore be billed for this service.\n\n\n------ Data collection ------\nYou can pick up the data in a portable hard drive (please notice the size of the data  is approximately XXXX GB).\n\nWe will keep a copy of the data for THREE MONTHS after the run date, and will then DELETE ALL OUR COPIES without further notice.\n\n\n------ Data output ------\nHere is an overview of your samples and the number of fragments that were sequenced:\n\n1-dummy_L002                       \t 197,112,378 fragments\n2-unit_L002                        \t 162,059,692 fragments\n3-element_L002                     \t 136,708,613 fragments\n4-test_L002                        \t 113,098,031 fragments\n5-datum_L002                       \t 110,208,932 fragments\n6-point_L002                       \t 117,902,689 fragments\n7-case_L002                        \t 105,886,244 fragments\n\n\n----- Bioinformatic analyses ----\nData alignment/analysis can be ordered as a service. For further details: http://www.sequencing.uio.no/services/bioinformatics/\n\nIf you have any questions, don't hesitate to get in touch. \n\n\n----- Technical details ----\nThe following run parameters and software versions were used to produce the data:\n\nSequencer Type: NovaSeqXPlus\nFlow Cell Type: 1.5B\n\nNovaSeqXPlus System Suite: 1.4.0.20115\nBCL Convert: 4.3.6\nNSC scripts: 3.0\n\n\nRegards\nArvind Sundaram / Marius Bj\u00f8rnstad\n\nBioinformatician(s)\nNorwegian Sequencing Centre (https://www.sequencing.uio.no) / Part of NorSeq (https://www.norseq.org/)\nOslo University Hospital, Ullev\u00e5l, Oslo, Norway\n\n\n*********************************************************************************************************************\nUnderstanding the data: https://www.sequencing.uio.no/illumina-services/10.%20Bioinformatic%20services/#toc9\n\n------- Acknowledgement -------\nThe Norwegian Sequencing Centre (NSC) operates as a core facility and you will therefore not be billed for the labour costs incurred. However, you are requested to acknowledge the support you have received from the bodies funding the NSC. Please use the following text in articles or reports relating to this sequence data:\n\"The sequencing service was provided by the Norwegian Sequencing Centre (www.sequencing.uio.no), a national technology platform hosted by the University of Oslo and Oslo University Hospital, and supported by the Research Council of Norway and the Southeastern Regional Health Authorities\".\n\n-----Terms, conditions and usage-----\nData storage policy: https://www.sequencing.uio.no/illumina-services/10.%20Bioinformatic%20services/#toc12\nData security:  https://www.sequencing.uio.no/illumina-services/10.%20Bioinformatic%20services/#toc11\n*********************************************************************************************************************\n\n",
                    "Open_emails.command": "#!/bin/bash\n\n# This shell script is written to the Delivery folder in\n# all runs processed by the demultiplexing scripts. It calls the AppleScript file\n# \"Open Emails.scpt\", which is located in /data/runScratch.boston/scripts.\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=$( dirname \"$0\" )\ncd \"$SCRIPT_DIR\"\nfor list_file in automatic_email_list-*.txt\ndo\n    osascript /Volumes/runScratch/scripts/Open\\ Emails.scpt \"$SCRIPT_DIR\" \"$list_file\"\ndone\n",
                    "automatic_email_list-260625_LH00534.A.Project_Example-test1-2026-07-28.txt": "text|||\"nsc-ous-data-delivery@sequencing.uio.no\" <nsc-ous-data-delivery@sequencing.uio.no>|Sequence ready for download - sequencing run 20260625_LH00534_0319_A22JKHGLT1 - Example-test1-2026-07-28 (9 samples)|260625_LH00534.A.Project_Example-test1-2026-07-28.txt|\n",
